I keep my note as part of the name of my original
primary weapon, so that I might have a quarterstaff
named:

  v1 sa2 vxx3 m4 o5 t7

meaning "vault on level 1, shop and co-aligned altar
on level 2, vault and two cross-aligned altars on
level 3, mines entrance on level 4, oracle on level
5, throne room on level 7". Since those names are of
quite limited length, I'd probably be better off to
keep the names on gems in a sack, but I like the
ease of adding notes to something in main inventory.

This way, I don't forget that the notes exist when I
restart my game, they're right there the first time
I do an inventory, which is always the first thing I
do anyway when I restart a game after a delay.

